That's because it will appear multiple times in the four entries of each small square.
So we put the integers in each of the not border octagons, say 1, 4,
3, and 8. And place four more integers so that each octagonal integer
is surrounded by the same integer.
Now we use a graphical algorithm that adds an integer 3 to each remaining
integer.
So from the current configuration:
[asy]
size(101);
draw(unitsquare);
draw(shift(up)*shift(right)*unitsquare);
filldraw(shift(up)*unitsquare,gray(.6));
